# NEVER normalise line endings in this repo. Not a style preference — a
# correctness requirement, and the failure it prevents is silent.
#
# occurrences/code-occurrences.csv is verified against the `csv_sha256` recorded
# in occurrence-summary.json before it is used, so that a hand-edited or
# half-transferred file cannot quietly become a number in a thesis table. That
# check is over BYTES. A git that rewrites CRLF to LF on commit — which
# `core.autocrlf=input` does, and it is a common global setting — changes those
# bytes without changing a single value, the sha256 check then fails, and
# common/occurrences.load() returns None.
#
# Nothing errors at that point, by design: absent occurrence counts are a
# legitimate state (they come from an HPC run). What actually happens is that
# the `not-observed-in-data` narrowing disappears, every code in an enumeration
# becomes mappable, and the ConceptMaps silently GROW. Measured, not
# hypothesised: a fresh clone of a normalising checkout produced maps with extra
# codes and every check still green.
#
# The committed blobs carry CRLF today. `git filter-repo` copies blobs verbatim
# so an extraction preserves them, but a later `git add` of the same file under
# `core.autocrlf=input` would not — which is what this file exists to stop.
